      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1270912819,
      "text": "Eremomastax speciosa is a species of flowering plant belonging to the family Acanthaceae.It is a subshrub or shrub native to tropical Africa, ranging from Guinea to Ethiopia, Zambia, and Madagascar. It is the sole species in genus Eremomastax."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Eremomastax speciosa",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eremomastax_speciosa",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 135212846,
      "text": "Eremomastax es un género monotípico de plantas con flores perteneciente a la familia Acanthaceae. Su única especie: Eremomastax speciosa (Hochst.) Cufod., es originaria de África."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Eremomastax speciosa",
